\par Similarly, in the Second Canto, the post-creation cosmic manifestation is described. The different plane
tary systems are described in the Second Canto as different parts of the universal body of the Lord. For this reason, the Second Canto can be called "The Cosmic Manifestation." There are ten chapters in the Second Canto, and in these ten chapters the purp
ose of }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 \'c7r\'e9mad}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
 and the different symptoms of this purpose are narrated. In the First Chapter, the glories of chanting are described, and the process of meditation on the universal form of the Lord by the neophyte}{\insrsid5596316  }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
devotees is hinted. In the first verse, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 replies to the questions of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, who asked him about one's duties at the point of his death. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it was glad to receive \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4
m\'e9, and he was proud of being a descendant of Arjuna, the intimate friend of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Personally, he was very humble and meek, but he expressed his gladness that Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba was very kind to the sons of }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid4592098 
P\'e4\'eb\'f2u}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 , or his grandfathers, especially his own grandfather, Arjuna. And because Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba is always pleased with his family, therefore, at the verge of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it's death, \'c7
ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 was sent to help him in the process of self-realization. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it was a devotee of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba from his childhood, so he had natural affection for K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 could 
understand his devotion to Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Therefore, he welcomed the questions about his duty. Because the King hinted that worship of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the ultimate function of every living entity, }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid4592098 \'c7ukadeva
}{\insrsid5596316  }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 Gosv\'e4m\'e9 welcomed the suggestion and said, "Because you have raised questions about K\'e5\'f1\'eba, your question is most glorious." The translation of the first verse is as follows.
