\'e0hit\'e4}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  (verse 48), it is said that all the universes and the heads of them (the }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid13907137 Brahm\'e4s}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
) exist only for the duration of His breathing period. The same is confirmed here. The air on which the universes and the planets within the universes exist is nothing but a bit of breathing of the unchallengeable }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid10317072 vir
\'e4\'f6a}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid11499196 puru\'f1a}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
. So even by studying the rivers, trees, air and the passing ages, one can conceive of the Personality of Godhead without being misled by the formless conception of the Lord. In the }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid4592098 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  (Bg. 12.5) it is stated that those who are much inclined to the formless conception of the Supreme Truth are more troubled than those who can intelligently conceive of the personal form.
