\'c7r\'e9la}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  \'c7ukadeva. He tries to impress upon us that instead of diverting our attention to several branches of self-realization, we
 should concentrate upon the Supreme Personality of Godhead as the supreme object of realization, worship and devotion. Self-realization is, as it were, offering a fight for eternal life against the material struggle for existence, and therefore by the il
lusory grace of the external energy, the }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 yogi}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  or the devotee is faced with many allurements which can entangle a great fighter again in the bondage of material existence. A }{
\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 yogi}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  can attain miraculous successes in the matter of material achievements, and they are called }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 a\'ebim\'e4}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 , }{
\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 laghim\'e4}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
, etc., by which one can become more minute than the minutest or lighter than the lightest, or in the ordinary sense, may achieve material benedictions in the shape of wealth and women. But he is warned against such allurements b
ecause to become again entangled in such illusory pleasure means degradation of the self and further imprisonment in the material world. By this warning, one should follow one's vigilant intelli}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 g}{
\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 ence only.
\par The Supreme Lord is one, and His expansions are va
rious. He is, therefore, the Supersoul of everything. When a man sees anything, he must know that his seeing is secondary and the Lord's seeing is primary. One cannot see anything without the Lord's having first seen it. That is the instruction of the }{
\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid6709237 Vedas}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  and the }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 Upani\'f1ads}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
. So whatever we see or do, the Supersoul of all acts of seeing or doing is the Lord. This theory of simultaneous oneness and difference between the individual soul and the Supersoul is propounded by Lord }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid4139932 \'c7r\'e9}{
\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  Caitanya }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid4592098 Mah\'e4prabhu}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  as the philosophy of }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 acintya}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 -}{
\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 bhed\'e4bheda}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid1071071 tattva}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 . The }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid10317072 vir\'e4\'f6a}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  }{
\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid12804399 r\'fcpa}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 , or the gigantic feature of the Supreme Lord, includes everything materially manifested, and therefore the }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid10317072 vir\'e4\'f6a}{
\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  or gigantic feature of the Lord is the Supersoul of all living and nonliving entities. But the }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid10317072 vir\'e4\'f6a}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid12804399 r
\'fcpa}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  is also the manifestation of }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid6709237 N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  or }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid3027206 Vi\'f1\'ebu}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
, and going further on and on one will eventually see that Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the ultimate Supersoul of everything that be. The conclusion is that one should unhesitatingly become a worshiper of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, or, for that matter, His plenary expansion, }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid6709237 N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 , and none else. In the Vedic hymns, it is clearly said that first of all }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid6709237 N\'e4r\'e4ya
\'eba}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  cast a glance over matter and thus there was creation. Before creation, there was neither }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid4139932 Brahm\'e4}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  nor }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid3027206 \'c7iva
}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 , and what to speak of others. }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 \'c7r\'e9p\'e4d}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 \'c7a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
 has definitely accepted this, that }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid6709237 N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
 is beyond the material creation and all others are within the material creation. The whole material creation is, therefore, one and different from }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid6709237 N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 , simulta}{
\insrsid5596316\charrsid7277327 n}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 eously, and this supports the philosophy of }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 acintya}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 bhed\'e4bheda}{
\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid1071071 tattva}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  of Lord }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid4139932 \'c7r\'e9}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787  Caitanya }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid4592098 Mah\'e4prabhu
}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 . Being an emanation from the glancing potency of }{\insrsid5596316\charrsid6709237 N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
, the whole material creation is nondifferent from Him. But because it is the effect of His external energy (}{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid16517566 bahira\'ecg\'e4}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid13907137 m\'e4y\'e4}{
\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 ) and is aloof from the internal potency (}{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid1071071 \'e4tma}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid13907137 m\'e4y\'e4}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 
), the whole material creation is different from Him at the same time. The example given in this verse very nicely is that of the dreaming man. The dreaming man creates many thin
gs in the dream, and thus he himself becomes the entangled seer of the dream and is also affected by the consequences. This material creation is also exactly a dream-like creation of the Lord, but He, being the transcendental Supersoul, is neither entangl
e
d nor affected by the reactions of such a dream-like creation. He is always in His transcendental position, but essentially He is everything, and nothing is apart from Him. One should therefore concentrate on Him only as His part and parcel without deviat
ion, otherwise one is sure to be overcome by the potencies of the material creation, one after another. It is confirmed in the }{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid4592098 Bhagavad}{\insrsid5596316\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid5596316\charrsid2833115 g\'e9t\'e4}{
