\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1641936 {\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 The necessities of life for the protection of the body, etc., must not be unnecessarily increased.
 Human energy is spoiled in a vain search after such illusory happiness. If one is able to lie down on the floor, then why should one endeavor to get a good bedstead or soft cushion to lie on? If one can rest without any pillow and make use of the soft ar
ms endowed by nature, there is no necessity of searching after a pillow. If we make a study of the general life of the animals, we can see that they have no intelligence to }{\insrsid1641936 build big houses, furniture, an}{
\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 d other household parapher}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid7277327 n}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 alia, and yet they maintai
n a healthy life by lying down on the open land. They do not know how to cook or prepare foodstuff, yet they still live healthy lives more easily than the human being. This does not mean that human civilization should revert to animal life nor that the hu
man being should live naked in the jungles without any culture, education, and sense of morality. An intelligent human cannot live the life of an animal}{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid4592098 ; }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
rather, man should try to utilize his intelligence in arts and science, poetry and philosophy. In such a way he can further the progressive march of human civilization. But here the idea given by }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid2833115 \'c7r\'e9la}{
\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  \'c7ukadeva }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid4139932 Gosv\'e4m\'e9}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
 is that the reserve energy of human life, far superior to that of animals, should simply be utilized for self-realization. Advancement of human civilization must be towards the goal of establish}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid15288099 i}{
\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 ng our lost relationship with God, which is not possible in any form of life other than the human. One must realize the nullity of the material phenomenon, considering it a passing phantasmagoria, and 
must endeavor to make a solution to the miseries of life. Self-complacence with a polished type of animal civilization geared to sense}{\insrsid1641936  gratification is delusion, and }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
such a "civilization" is not worthy of the name. In pursuit of such false activities, a human being is in the clutches of }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid13907137 m\'e4y\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
, or illusion. Great sages and saints in the days of yore were not living in palatial buildings furnished with good furniture and so-called amenities of life. They used to live in huts and groves and sit on the flat grou
nd, and yet they have left immense treasures of high knowledge with all perfection. }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid2833115 \'c7r\'e9la}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid12459183 R\'fcpa}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  }{
