\par There is an intimate relationship between the swan and the lotus stem. So the comparison is very appropriate: without becoming a swan or }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid609507 paramaha\'e0sa}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
, one cannot enter into the network of the lotus feet of the Lord. The mental speculators, as it is stated in the }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid15288099 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
, even by dint of learned scholarship, cannot even dream of the Absolute Truth by speculating 
over it for eternity. The Lord reserves the right of not being exposed to such mental speculators. And because they cannot enter into the network stem of the lotus feet of the Lord, all mental speculators differ in conclusions, and at the end they make a 
useless compromise by saying "as many conclusions, as many ways," according to one's own inclination (}{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid12676904 yath\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid14381883 rucam}{
\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 ). But the Lord is not like a shopkeeper trying to please all sorts of customers in the mental speculator exchange. The Lord is what He is, the 
Absolute Personality of Godhead, and He demands absolute surrender unto Him only. The pure devotee, however, by following the ways of previous }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid3027206 \'e4c\'e4ryas}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
 or authorities, can see the Supreme Lord through the transparent medium of a bona fide spiritual master (}{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid14381883 anupa\'e7yanti}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
). The pure devotee never tries to see the Lord by mental speculation, but by following the footsteps of the }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid3027206 \'e4c\'e4ryas}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  (}{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid14381883 mah\'e4jano yena gata
\'f9 sa panth\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 ). Therefore there is no difference of conclusions amongst the }{\insrsid1641936 Vai\'f1\'ebava}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid3027206 \'e4c\'e4ryas}{
\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  regarding the Lord and the devotees. Lord Caitanya asserts that the living entity (}{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid946729 j\'e9va}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
) is eternally the servitor of the Lord and that he is simultaneously one and different from the Lord. This }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid1071071 tattva}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  of Lord Caitanya is shared by all the four }{
\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid4665559 samprad\'e4yas}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  of the }{\insrsid1641936 Vai\'f1\'ebava}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  s
chool (all accepting eternal servitude of the Lord even after salvation), and there is no authorized }{\insrsid1641936 Vai\'f1\'ebava}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid1574815 \'e4c\'e4rya}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
 who may think of the Lord and himself as one.
\par This humbleness of the pure devotee who is one hundred percent engaged in His service puts the devotee of the Lord in a trance to realize everything, because to the sincere devotee of the Lord, the Lord reveals Himself, as it is stated in the }{
\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid4592098 Bhagavad}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid2833115 g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  (Bg. 10.10). The Lord, being the Lord of intelligence in everyone (even in the nondevotee), 
favors His devotee with proper intelligence so that automatically the pure devotee is enlightened with the factual truth about the Lord and His different energies. The Lord is revealed not by one's speculative power or by one's verbal jugglery over the Ab
solute Truth. Rather, He reveals Himself to a devotee when He is fully satisfied by his service attitude. \'c7ukadeva }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid4139932 Gosv\'e4m\'e9}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
 is not a mental speculator or compromiser of the theory of "as many ways, as many conclusions," but He prays to the Lord only, invoking His transcendental pleasure. That is the way of knowing the Lord.
