's becoming all-powerful is a lesson for the frogs in the well, that they may not be bewildered in misconceiving the identity of the Person}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid13905572 a}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
lity of Godhead (even by comparison with a personality like }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid4139932 Brahm\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 , so what to speak of ordinar
y men who falsely pose themselves as God or an incarnation of God). The Supreme Lord is always the Supreme, and as we have tried to establish many times in these purports, no living being, even up to the standard of }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid4139932 Brahm
\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 , can claim to be one with the Lord. One should not be misled when people worship a great man as God after his death as a matter of hero worship. There were many kings like Lord }{\insrsid1641936 R\'e4macandra}{
\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 , the King of }{\insrsid1641936 Ayodhy\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 , but none of them are mentioned as God in the revealed scriptures. To become a good king is not necessarily the qualification of becoming Lord }
{\insrsid1641936 R\'e4ma}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 , but to be a great personality like K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the qualification of becoming the Personality of Godhead. If we scrutinize the characters who took part in the Battle of }{\insrsid1641936 
