\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1641936 {\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
The Personality of Godhead is the supreme master of everything auspicious because the results of whatever actions are performed by the living being, either in the material or spiritual existence, are awarded by the Lord. As such, He is the ultimate ben
efactor. Every individual living entity is unborn, and therefore even after the annihilation of the material elementary body, the living entity exists, exactly like the air within the body.
\par 
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1641936 {\insrsid1641936\charrsid8139127 PURPORT}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1641936 {\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 The living entity is unborn and eternal, and as it is confirmed in the }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid4592098 Bhagavad-g\'e9t
\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
 (Bg. 2.30), the living entity is not exhausted even though the material elementary body is vanquished. As long as the living entity is in the material existence, actions performed by him are rewarded in the next life, or even in
 the present life. Similarly, in his spiritual life also actions are rewarded by the Lord by the five kinds of liberation. Even the impersonalist cannot achieve the desired merging into the existence of the Supreme without being favored by the Supreme Per
sonality of Godhead. It is confirmed in the }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid4592098 Bhagavad}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid2833115 g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
 also (Bg. 4.11) that the Lord awards similar results, as one desires, in one's present life. The living entities are given freedom to make their choice, and}{\insrsid1641936  the Lord awards them accordingly.}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
\par It is the duty of everyone, therefore, to worship devoutly only the Personality of Godhead to achieve his desired goal. The impersonalist,}{\insrsid1641936  }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
instead of speculating or meditating, can directly execute the routine devotional service of the Lord and thus easily obtain the desired goal.
\par The devotees, however, are naturally inclined to become associates of the Lord without being merged in the spiritual existence, as conceived by the impersonalist. The devotees, therefore, following their constitutional instincts, achieve 
the desired goal of becoming servitors, friends, fathers, mothers or conjugal lovers of the Lord. The devotional service of the Lord involves nine transcendental processes of hearing and chanting, etc., and by performing such easy and natural devotional s
ervices the devotees achieve the highest perfectional results, far, far superior to merging into the existence of the }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid14252554 Brahman}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
. The devotees are, therefore, never advised to indulge in speculating upon the nature of the Supreme, or artificially meditating on the void.
\par One should not, however, misunderstand that after the annihilation of this present body there is no body by which one can associate with the Lord face to face. The living entity is unborn. It is not that he is manifest with the creation of the m
aterial body. On the other hand, it is true that the material body develops only by the desire of the living entity. The evolution of the material body is due to such desires of the living being. According to the desires of the living being, the material 
b
ody develops. So from the spirit soul the material body comes into existence, generated from the living force. As the living being is eternal, so he exists just like the air within the body. Air is within and without the body. Therefore when the external 
c
overing, the material body, is vanquished, the living spark, like the air within the body, continues to exist. And by the direction of the Lord, because He is the ultimate benefactor, the living entity is at once awarded the necessary spiritual body befit
ting his association with the Lord in the manner of }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid9072955 s\'e4r\'fcpya}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  (equal bodily feature), }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid9072955 s\'e4lokya}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
 (equal facility to live in the same planet with the Lord), }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid14819760 s\'e4r\'f1\'f6i}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  (equal possession of opulence like the Lord), and }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid14819760 s\'e4m\'e9pya}{
\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  (equal association with the Lord).
\par The Lord is so kind that even if a devotee of the Lord cannot fulfill the complete course of devotional ser}{\insrsid1641936 vice unalloyed and uncontaminate}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 
d by material association, he is given another chance in the next life by being awarded a birth in the family of a devotee 
or rich man so that without being engaged in the struggle for material existence, the devotee can finish the remaining purification of his existence and thus immediately, after relinquishing the present body, go back home, back to Godhead. This is confirm
ed in the }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid4592098 Bhagavad}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 -}{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid2833115 g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 .
\par In this connection detailed information is available in the }{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid14819760 Bhagavat}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid14819760 -}{\i\insrsid1641936\charrsid16602255 sandarbha}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  of }{\insrsid1641936 \'c7r\'e9la
}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid946729 J\'e9va}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  }{\insrsid1641936\charrsid4139932 Gosv\'e4m\'e9}{\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787  }{\insrsid1641936 Prabhup\'e4da}{
\insrsid1641936\charrsid16332787 . Once achieving the spiritual existence, the devotee is eternally situated there, as already discussed in the previous verse.
