, the science of devotional service, one should not eat more than what he requires to maintain body and soul together. Vegetable diets and milk are suf
ficient for maintenance of the human body, and therefore one has no need to eat anything more to satisfy the palate. One should also not accumulate money to become puffed up in the material world. One should earn his livelihood easily and honestly, for it
